# CODEOWNERS — founder review where authority lives, and nowhere else.
#
# Rule: a path is listed here only if a change to it can change WHO may act or
# WHAT money may move — constitutional files, the gates that enforce authority,
# the money/identity registry packages, and the authority doors outside
# packages/. Everything else (docs, UI, tests, tooling) is CI-only. There is
# deliberately NO catch-all `*` line: with code-owner review required by the
# ruleset, `*` would gate every PR.
#
# GitHub semantics: the LAST matching pattern wins; a pattern with no owner
# makes matching paths unowned. Why-comments sit on the line ABOVE each entry:
# GitHub skips any line it cannot parse, so no trailing comments.
#
# Drift gate: scripts/check-codeowners-authority.ts (`pnpm check`). It derives
# the required set from scripts/money-identity-path.ts (MONEY_IDENTITY_PATH),
# the identity-authority writers gate and the money-authority gate, and fails
# if any of those paths is not owned here or a catch-all appears. Section (C)
# entries no existing gate tracks live ONLY in this file.

